==Strategy==
==='''Chapters 1 & 2'''===
Not too hard of a stage. Make sure the [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] burrow early so they don't get right up to your base. Get your [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] ready for the main threats and try to keep units flowing so that you don't get caught off guard by more burrowing Zombies.

All in all, not a terribly tough stage, but any [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] and [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien units]] will be super helpful.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Bring as many [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie units]] as possible and as many as 5 meatshields. Most enemies in this stage do massive amounts of damage, so having more cheap meatshields ([[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Samba]]) will be better than fewer more powerful meatshields (i.e. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Commando]], etc.) due to money efficiency. Li'l Zyclone does very little damage per hit by comparison, but his job is just to soak up meatshields and block for his longer-ranged allies.

[[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cat]] is a god-send on this stage because of the near perma-freeze you will achieve on Li'l Zyclone and Zomboe when you have a couple of them stacked up. In fact, Li'l Zyclone is probably the easiest part of the stage in the grand scheme of things. If you survive the initial wave AND survive the boss shockwave with units ready to spawn then it shouldn't be too tough. You can't really do the [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] rush strategy on this stage due to the Cyberhorn and the massive amount of Shibaliens that spawn with him. With [[Treasure]]s and many [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer units]], you should have little trouble after the initial lineup. Once the Li'l Zyclone is down for good, finish off the Cyberhorn and Shibaliens for the victory.

